{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["Trees"]}],"extendedModule":"Trees","title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertex"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L38","fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift"},"externalID":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV12GraphDrawingE21reingoldTilfordLayoutAD0E0VyxGyF","role":"symbol"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reingoldTilfordLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly. A mirrored tree draws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the reflection of the drawing, and isomorphic subtrees are drawn identically up to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"translation. Separations and centring give multiples of a power of ½, which are exact in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":". The even spacing divides a shift by the number of gaps, so values such as ±5\/6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"occur and are rounded, and a mirrored tree’s drawing then matches the reflection only to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rounding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Experience 20(7), 1990."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing":{"role":"collection","title":"GraphDrawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees/RootedTree":{"title":"RootedTree","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV","text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees","abstract":[],"title":"Trees"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Drawing":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/drawing","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A position in the plane for each vertex, in a fixed vertex order: what every layout in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module returns, and what a caller passes as a starting drawing.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees/RootedTree/reingoldTilfordLayout()":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form."}],"title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reingoldTilfordLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}}}